        >>[x] Keep written-id records when reading a named template =chst-reader $One small reviewed run of the =chst-rebrief split; worker and independent reviewer from different vendors. Named tests first, run red and proven to execute (not a zero-test filtered pass); clearhead-core/scripts/gate.sh passes before landing. Run chst1's workspace (agent run 20261105-133227) is evidence, not a base: start from main. Why: stamping must refuse a step with no written #uuid (linting.md, Habit scope and template warnings: missing template-step ids block stamping and are reported for explicit minting), and chst1 could not, because clearhead-cli/src/filesystem/templates.rs read_template_actions goes through clearhead_core::parse_actions, which returns only the ActionList and drops ParsedDocument.source_map's is_id_generated. What: the named-template reader returns its steps together with which ones had a written id, from the parser's record, never a flag a caller passes; its callers (cli/template.rs, cli/charter.rs, filesystem/calendar.rs) keep their behaviour. The habit-id-missing report in workspace/habit_files.rs covers named-template steps as it covers inline children. Acceptance: habit_template_ids tests: a named template step without #uuid is reported and identifiable from the reader's output; written ids round-trip unchanged; inline children still reported as today. Out of scope: stamping, where templates are looked up (=charter-local-templates is open), times. IMPLEMENTED in run chrd1, not yet landed: Core tests 6d2be36, implementation 73952d5; named reader returns strict ParsedDocument with parser source_map.is_id_generated, and three callers keep behavior through .actions. habit-id-missing covers named template steps and inline children. Retrospective red evidence accepted by independent review /6: unchanged Core test-only commit 6d2be367b9f6d6634a66a118dc816d2d436ab2d8 ran cargo test -p clearhead_core --test habit_template_ids -- --nocapture; all 3 executed, 2 pass