[ ] Move charter logs out of the charter file =charter-log-file $From the philosopher, 2026-10-22, talked through with Darrion. Problem: the charter Log section is the one record ClearHead keeps in the live file; completed actions move to .completed.actions and closed charters to archive/, outside the default read. A rough keyword sort of 131 jots in 17 charters across projects: about 52 action outcomes, 21 decisions, 9 findings, 49 other. srr's charter is 2,065 of 2,080 words log; the assistant's is 691 of 2,856, read at every wake. Proposal: (1) jot writes to a log file beside the charter, named by the charter stem, which joins the known files that archive moves with the charter; show charter prints the core only. (2) An action's outcome is a log entry that references it, not a result field: complete --note writes one, and show action lists entries referencing it. jot resolves a reference when written and refuses an ambiguous one, since aliases can be reused. (3) orient shows each active charter's size, a number and not a limit. Open, Darrion's call: the log format, a markdown list in today's entry grammar or ndjson. Evidence: ~/Products/philosopher docs/charter-anatomy.md and log.md.$ +philosopher ^2026-10-22T09:26 #01a162ef-5bc0-7142-8c81-06b58754d1c5
[ ] Align the legacy root Topiary query with canonical formatting =grammar-legacy-formatting $Found by grammar-habits worker in sandbox 20261025-050329 and confirmed by Claude review. Legacy tree-sitter-actions/queries/actions.scm removes spaces before names and @ or due metadata; canonical queries/actions/formatting.scm and queries/actions/actions.scm retain expected spaces. Decide at implementation level whether to retire the legacy entry point or align it with canonical queries, and add coverage. No recurrence regression; do not weaken canonical formatting expectations. Original sandbox finding id 01a17176-6447-7983-8a3b-1eed4a784f4d was not landed because its platform commit bundled unpublished gitlinks; this action is its durable main-branch replacement.$ ^2026-10-25T06:09 #01a171ad-e21a-7a82-bce1-fe0e9d96e8d6
