    >[x] Follow the new close in clearhead.nvim =ci-nvim $Step 3 of =close-individually, against the Core release from =ci-core. As docs/close-individually-proposal.md What changes item 3 says: fix set_state_tree so a closed child is not overwritten (Core Decision 2, as amended for cascade: closed members keep state and date, the target is forced), add :Clearhead unarchive, and document the verbs including the sweep-back: with nvim_archive_on_save on, a plain unarchive holds only until the next save, by design. nvim_archive_on_save itself is unchanged. Move the pin in this branch.  Core is released as v0.4.0 (platform pin 09c0990); the sandbox builds that CLI from the pin, so no Core change belongs here. Core now refuses any file containing R: as a parse error; nvim needs nothing for that in this cycle. Workflow run cin1 (2026-11-05), worker gpt-6.1-sol on ChatGPT, review claude-opus-5-5. The landing push of clearhead.nvim waits on =nvim-push-hook. Implemented in clearhead.nvim 1df7646 (regressions, including correction of the earlier cancellation-date expectation) and 53fd61d (implementation/docs). Close cascades force a changed target with a fresh date, keep same-state target dates and all closed-member states/dates, and reach open grandchildren through closed members. Added :Clearhead unarchive action with CLI flags forwarded, synchronous execution, unsaved-action-buffer protection, and clean-buffer refresh without saving. Documented single versus cascade close/reopen, whole-root archive/unarchive, composed reopen flags, and intentional next-save sweep-back; nvim_archive_on_save is unchanged. Tested against pinned Core v0.4.0 (09c0990): full Neovim suite 79/79 with the real pinned grammar and CLI; full Core gate green before each commit. No Core change or new dependencies. Platform plugin pin moves in this branch; landing push still waits on =nvim-push-hook.$ !2 ^2026-11-02T02:43 %2026-11-05T02:02 <ci-core #01a19a23-87cb-7773-ae27-d656b3fb2821
