[ ] Merge .actions files three ways by action UUID, as a git merge driver and a plain command =semantic-merge $Decided 2026-11-04 (Darrion): in the first usable iteration; a generic tool anyone can use, cashing in the format's per-line UUIDs. Two problems share the root: agent-sandbox's =claim-guard freezes a whole repo during a writer session because landings conflicted on .actions files the host also edited (srr next.actions, 2026-10-10), and Syncthing leaves conflict copies (personal-os =syncthing-merge). Line-based merges conflict on neighbouring lines that are independent records. Builds on what Core has: diff_actions (UUID-keyed added, removed, modified with field changes, used by the LSP) and patch_action_list (a two-way overlay behind clearhead patch file). Missing: a base-aware three-way merge with per-field conflicts, parent and order changes (diff tracks neither), lines without UUIDs, and an entry point git can call as a merge driver (%O %A %B, non-zero exit and readable markers on a true conflict) that the Syncthing watcher also calls. Acceptance: named tests for neighbouring edits, the same action changed in different fields, the same field changed on both sides (a conflict), add on one side and complete on the other, reparent and reorder, and no line duplicated or lost; then the claim guard can narrow to true conflicts (agent-sandbox follow-up). Spec: whether merge semantics belong in specifications is Darrion's call when the worker reaches it.$ !2 ^2026-11-04T08:02 #01a1a594-7bdf-7aa2-b945-05e8e111207a
